# nsMsgProgress::OnStatus behavior in mailnews/base/src/nsMsgProgress.cpp

Copies statusArg into a host string and uses FormatStatusMessage to localize the network status. Propagates formatting errors. On success, obtains Feedback service and reports UTF8 message with empty operation ID when service exists. It does not call OnStatusChange or update this object's pending status.

## State read

- aStatus; aStatusArg; request unused

## State changed

- Local strings; feedback service may change external state

## Calls and triggers

- FormatStatusMessage maps status to Fluent ID, named host argument and netwerk/necko.ftl atnsMsgUtils.cpp:606-666.
- mozilla::components::Feedback::Service()->ReportStatus; concrete feedback implementation not read.

## Result and consumers

Formatting failure returns its nsresult. Otherwise NS_OK, even when Feedback service unavailable or ReportStatus fails.

## Errors

NS_ENSURE_SUCCESS short-circuits formatting failure; ReportStatus return ignored.

## Async completion

Synchronous formatting/call; downstream feedback processing completion not established.

## Ownership and cleanup

Local smart pointer retains Feedback service during call; no retained request or host.

